+#### Finding G1-1: Nested Concurrency Lockout Does Not Measure Multi-Threaded Cross-Core Schedules
+- **Path**: `docs/library/proof/worker-bootstrap-owner-2026-09-13/worker-bootstrap-owner-instrument01/runs/wbo01/owned_generation_protocol.py`
+- **Line**: 296–304 (`_factory_operation`) and 179–192 (`_operation`)
+- **Trigger**: Single-threaded nested re-entry into `build_factory_product` or `release_factory_product` while `_factory_active` is true.
+- **Consequence**: `RuntimeOwnerRefusal("factory_operation_already_active")` is raised synchronously. While this guarantees serial re-entrancy protection, it does not measure or test true cross-thread contention, thread scheduling races, lock convoying, or OS kernel thread preemption.
+- **Smallest Repair / Missing Observation**: Document the concurrency scope as single-thread re-entrancy lockout. A future multi-threaded qualification suite exercising concurrent worker threads against shared channels is required to validate true cross-thread safety.
