+## Group 2: Windows Journal, Recovery and Source Invariants
+
+### 1. Trace of Physical Identity, Handle Exclusions, Short I/O, and Poisoning
+- **Physical Identity vs Semantic Aliases**: In `docs/library/proof/windows-reservation02-2026-09-13/author/test_windows_reservations.py#L380-L405` (`test_physical_gate_ignores_semantic_aliases`), physical gate identity is bound to `(volume_serial, file_id)`. Two distinct semantic paths resolving to the same underlying physical file ID share the exact same gate; differing physical files with identical semantic labels receive separate gates.
+- **Exclusive Handle Ownership & Ancestor/Share Exclusions**:
+  - In `windows_reservation_port.py#L48-L82`, files are opened with Win32 sharing flags excluding write/delete sharing (`FILE_SHARE_READ` only or exclusive).
+  - Ancestor directory chains are validated via `_checked_chain()` in `trusted_asr_resolver.py#L205-L215`, rejecting symlinks (`stat.S_ISLNK`), reparse points (`0x400`), and path aliases before resolution.
+- **Short I/O Handling**: In `test_windows_reservations.py#L350-L378` (`test_short_native_writes_complete_exact_journal`), simulated partial native writes complete the full required byte count in a loop without truncating the journal record.
+- **Poisoned Uncertainty**: In `windows_reservation_port.py#L118-L195`, any low-level seek, read, write, flush, or identity failure immediately sets `self.poisoned = True`. Once poisoned:
+  - All subsequent read, write, or truncate operations raise `KernelUnconfirmed("stream_is_poisoned")`.
+  - The exclusive handle is retained to prevent foreign access to corrupted state.
+- **Flush / Readback & Revision-Bound Clean Confirmation**:
+  - In `windows_reservation_port.py#L170-L195`, writes update `self._revision`. Clean head confirmation caches `self.confirmed_clean_head` bound to `self.confirmed_revision`.
+  - In `test_windows_reservations.py#L425-L445` (`test_write_revision_invalidates_previous_confirmation`), a subsequent write increments `_revision`, immediately invalidating the clean cache.
+- **Transition Lock Scope vs Journal Flush**:
+  - In `snapshot_reservations.py#L140-L190`, `ReservationService._transition()` acquires `self._lock` when updating internal reservation token state.
+  - However, journal flushes are performed outside the manager state lock (`test_reservations.py#L650-L671`, `test_journal_sync_never_holds_manager_state_lock`), ensuring I/O latency does not block unrelated lifecycle state transitions.
+- **Private Transition Caller Exclusions**:
+  - `_transition()` serializes state machine transitions for callers of `ReservationService`.
+  - **Critical Invariant Boundary**: This serialization applies strictly to callers utilizing `_transition()`. It does **not** exclude conflicting operations if external threads or direct stream handles bypass `ReservationService` and invoke stream operations directly.
+- **Ordinary Clear vs Live Reconciliation**:
+  - In `snapshot_reservations.py#L380-L420`, ordinary clear requires confirmed clean durability before gate release.
+  - Live reconciliation (`reconcile_live`) renews durability of an already-cleared or quarantined head without permitting ordinary reuse.
+
