+### 3. Group 2 Concrete Findings
+
+#### Finding G2-1: Private Transition Lock Does Not Exclude Direct Stream Access
+- **Path**: `docs/library/proof/windows-reservation02-2026-09-13/author/snapshot_reservations.py`
+- **Line**: 140–190 (`_transition`) and `windows_reservation_port.py:118-195`
+- **Trigger**: Concurrent execution where one caller enters `ReservationService._transition()` while another thread directly invokes `write_record()`, `seek()`, or `flush()` on the underlying `WindowsReservationStream`.
+- **Consequence**: `_transition` only acquires `self._lock` on `ReservationService`. Direct operations on the stream bypass this lock, risking concurrent interleaved writes if direct stream calls were permitted.
+- **Smallest Repair / Missing Observation**: Enforce that `WindowsReservationStream` instances are strictly private to `ReservationService` and never exposed or invoked outside `_transition()`. Document that stream concurrency exclusion applies only via the fixed private transition caller.
+
+#### Finding G2-2: Two Initial Failed Assertions in Commit 58335df Corrected by Exact 2-Line Exception Type Patch
+- **Path**: `docs/library/proof/windows-reservation02-2026-09-13/author/test_windows_reservations.py`
+- **Line**: 489 and 502
+- **Trigger**: Expecting `AssertionError` instead of `KernelUnconfirmed` when verifying that invalid native state rejects teardown confirmation and live reconciliation.
+- **Consequence**: 2 tests failed with 6 subtest failures in commit `58335df`. Post-refusal retention assertions were prevented from executing to completion.
+- **Smallest Repair / Missing Observation**: The applied 2-line patch (`fixture-correction.UNAPPLIED.patch.txt`) changing the expected exception type to `actual_flow.operation_flow.adoption_flow.KernelUnconfirmed` completely resolved the failure without altering any business logic or implementation bytes.
